    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0586" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.857 L 97/126½a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Colonel E. M. House
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-11T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1916—6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 2. <hi rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi> case progressing. Satisfactory
                    settlement probable. Germany apparently believes if case settled it will leave
                    only matters with Great Britain unsettled and some action will be necessary.</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
